; implies_index_out_of_range: the same bound on the opcode that writes both
; surfaces.
;
; IMPLIES adds a linear term at i and a quadratic one at (i, j), so an
; unbounded i reached the linear map as well as the quadratic one -- the case
; EXCLUDE cannot cover. i is therefore the out-of-range operand here, where
; exclude_index_out_of_range puts it on j.

PUSH 4
BQMX r0

PUSH 100         ; i, far past the extent
PUSH 2           ; j, in range
PUSH 1           ; penalty
IMPLIES r0
HALT
